-- title:
--   The pruned thin-product program at c = 21.2733, θ = 0.111731 solves the thin matrix product on all instances
-- statement:
--   Procedure $74$ (`allInstancesF`) of the program `programF` solves the thin matrix product task `thinTask` within `allInstancesTimeF c₃₀` steps and with need `allInstancesNeedF`:
--
--   for an instance $x$ with parameters $N, D, w, U$ (two integer matrices $X\in\mathbb Z^{N\times D}$, $Y\in\mathbb Z^{D\times N}$ with entries bounded by $U$ and $w$ wanted positions $(i_k,j_k)$), the call writes the $w$ entries $\sum_{t<D}X_{i_k t}Y_{t j_k}$ to the output area and changes no other cell below the free pointer. The time is $30000+t_{\mathrm{off}}(N,D,w)$ when $D^{1249}\le N^{71}$, where $t_{\mathrm{off}}$ is the time `tOffline32P` of the offline routine of Corollary 32 with pruned encodings at the rational parameters `ratParamsF` ($c=212733/10000$, $\theta=111731/10^6$), and $30000+40(w+1)(D+1)$ (brute force) otherwise.
--
--   `programF` is `program31P ratParamsF` (the programs of Section 4 with pruned encodings, Corollaries 31-32) followed by `allInstancesF` (number 74), which tests $D^{1249}\le N^{71}$ with `regimeTestF` (number 75).
--
--   “Procedure $p$ of program $P$ solves the task within $T$ steps with need $\nu$” (`SolvesN`) means: in every program that begins with $P$, for every instance and every memory satisfying the task's precondition, and all limits (word size, cells, call depth) allowing $\nu$ of the instance's parameters, the call of $p$ with the instance's arguments ends within $T$ of the parameters steps and leaves a memory satisfying the postcondition.
